  "description": "KEKLUL crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C68 H54 Br8 N8 O13 Tb4,0.5(C3 H10 N2 O1),C2 H3 N1,1.25(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.610-4.908 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.32-173.39°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Tb4(μ4-O)(HL)2(L)2]·0.5(H2NCH2CHOHCH2NH2)·(CH3CN)·1.25(H2O) (H3L = 1,3-bis(5-bromosalicylideneamino)-2-propanol). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
